# fixedbugs, defect 2321, 2026-11-07: `a` declared as an `i64` and again as
# a `str`, built naming it once with a `str`. It was told the construction
# missed `a:, a:` and the value's type. Now the construction is read against
# the first declaration, the one the refusal leaves standing and the one a
# read `r.a` takes, so the type is told alone: as `r.a` would be an `i64`,
# so is the value a construction gives it.
record R
    a: i64
    a: str  #~ field_declared_twice

function main()
    r = R(a: "one")  #~ type_mismatch
    print(r.a)
